{"id":"24.01.TriangleAlien","contentHtml":"<p>This project is based on my original idea — to create a dynamic arcade game, the gameplay of which takes place on a procedurally generated 3D track.</p>\n<p>As a <mark>Solo Developer</mark>, I was responsible for <strong>100%</strong> of all aspects: from designing and implementing core technology to game design, creating all art, animation, and sound design.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>Challenge</h2>\n<p>The main task was to implement the game world as a procedural 3D \"ribbon\", <strong>the geometry of which is used by a custom shader to \"cut out\" everything outside of it</strong>.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>Engineering Solution</h2>\n<p>To realize this vision, I developed and integrated several complex systems that together form a unique gaming experience.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Procedural Generation of World \"Ribbon\" (CPU):</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Created a system from scratch that <mark>builds a complex 3D mesh along a Bezier guide curve</mark>. This mesh is the \"ribbon\" — the visible and playable part of the world.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Dynamic World \"Cutting\" (GPU):</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Wrote a custom shader that uses the geometry of the generated \"ribbon\" as a mask in the <code>Stencil Buffer</code> to <strong>\"cut out\" everything outside of it</strong> in real-time.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Shader Customization System:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Created a second custom shader allowing <mark>instantly changing the color palette of the entire game</mark>. All assets were pre-prepared with RGB channel marking, which allowed implementing deep customization without duplicating textures.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Gameplay Born from Technology:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>The visual effect of <strong>\"cutting\"</strong> formed the basis of the key mechanic of seamless <strong>\"teleportation\"</strong> of obstacles.</li>\n<li>On this basis, a full-fledged <code>one-finger</code> gameplay was developed, including enemy behavior logic (homing bullets) and a <strong>full-fledged meta-game</strong> (<code>store with 10+ skins</code>, <code>Daily Gifts</code>).</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Full Production Cycle:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>The entire visual style, from vector graphics to <code>VFX</code>, was created by me. The character received skeletal animation, a <code>state machine</code> of states, and procedural animation of the eye tracking the nearest target.</li>\n<li>To create a unique atmosphere, I <strong>personally recorded and processed all voice acting</strong> for the character.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<hr>\n<h2>Outcome</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Technology Implemented:</strong> A unique pipeline where a procedural mesh controls rendering via a custom shader successfully became the core of the product.</li>\n<li><strong>Holistic Product:</strong> Alone brought the game from idea to release, completing 100% of the work — from code and shaders to art and sound.</li>\n<li><strong>Deep Expertise:</strong> The project confirmed mastery of <mark>procedural generation of 3D meshes and writing custom shaders</mark> to create technologically complex products.</li>\n</ul>\n","published":true,"title":"Triangle Alien","date":"2024-01","type":"project","tagsArray":["Mobile","Arcade","Unity","C#","Illustrator","Photoshop","HLSL","VFX","Zenject (Extenject)","UniTask","Odin Inspector","DOTween"],"heroVideo":["NmBrzRLxU1c"],"shortDescription":"<p>Solo project built on the synergy of two technologies: <strong>procedural 3D track generation</strong> and a custom shader that <mark>“carves out” the game world</mark> along their shape.</p>\n","storeLinks":["https://grindset.space/"],"role":"solo","projectIcon":"/images/projects/24.01.TriangleAlien/icon.webp","cardBackground":"/images/projects/24.01.TriangleAlien/card.video?v=1765111352483&webm=1&mp4=1","screenshots":[{"src":"/images/projects/24.01.TriangleAlien/screenshots/1.webp","width":1080,"height":1920},{"src":"/images/projects/24.01.TriangleAlien